  "name": "Banda de pífanos (Northeastern cane-fife band)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Instrumental band tradition of the Northeastern agreste and sertão, also called zabumba or terno de pífanos, playing for saints' novenas, processions and festas: two cane fifes (pífanos) carry the tune in parallel over zabumba, snare drum and cymbals. The best-known group, the Banda de Pífanos de Caruaru of the Biano family, has made a long series of commercial records. The credited bamboo-flute card stands in for the cane pífano and a generic membrane-drum card for the zabumba bass drum.",
